ype": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "If you have ever tried to grow plants, you know that plants need a warm environment. For this reason, plants are being grown in glass greenhouses. The glass traps the warm air inside so that the plants can grow.<br/>\nThis happens on the earth as well. Gases found naturally in the atmosphere trap the heat of the sun, and warm up the earth to a comfortable 59 degrees Fahrenheit. This has been called the \"greenhouse effect\", which makes it possible for humans, animals, and plants to live. If there were no gases in the atmosphere, the earth would be a frozen snowball.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": ""}, {"text": "Many scientists say that human activities have caused greenhouse gases, such as carbon dioxide, to build up in the atmosphere. According to this theory, whenever we burn fossil fuels, such as gasoline, oil, coal, or natural gas, more greenhouse gases are being released into the atmosphere. As a result, the atmosphere is trapping more heat, and the earth is warming up. This theory is known as global warming.", "id": 2, "time": "37500", "image": ""}, {"text": "Some scientists claim that global warming will take generations to affect the earth. Others predict that if we do not reduce the release of greenhouse gases now, global temperatures will rise several degrees within the next 100 years. This change in temperature could mean major climate changes throughout the world.<br/>\nScientists claim that if we had acted earlier, humankind wouldn't have found themselves in this predicament. Once greenhouse gases have been released into the atmosphere, most of them remain there for decades and continue to trap heat.", "id": 3, "time": "66500", "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn9le02ob03re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "_data": [], "type": "video", "template_override": 1}]}]}